This project builds on OrganoID.

    OrganoID: a versatile deep learning platform for tracking and analysis of
    single-organoid dynamics.
    Matthews, J. M., Schuster, B., Kashaf, S. S., et al.
    PLoS Computational Biology 18(11): e1010584 (2022).
    Source: https://github.com/jono-m/OrganoID

The OrganoID U-Net architecture, its training routine, its image preprocessing,
its belief-map forward pass, and its 2-D post-processing are used essentially
unchanged. OrganoID's source is NOT copied into this repository; it is referenced
as a git submodule under `organoid_tf/`. All rights to the OrganoID code remain
with its original authors under the terms of that repository.

What this repository adds on top of OrganoID (original work, MIT-licensed — see
LICENSE):

  * a large-organoid training supplement and a two-stage fine-tuning launcher;
  * a format-agnostic image reader (`app/io/volume_source.py`) supporting Nikon
    ND2 and OME-TIFF / ImageJ / plain TIFF inputs;
  * per-Z segmentation with greedy-IoU Z-stitching for 3-D organoid identity;
  * a greedy 3-D volumetric-IoU time tracker with gap-closing (replacing
    OrganoID's 2-D Hungarian tracker for this 3-D use case);
  * ROI-as-post-hoc-selection, split-detection merging, and inclusion filters;
  * a 3-D metric suite (trapezoidal-integrated volume, background-subtracted
    per-channel fluorescence intensities);
  * a headless, crash-safe, resumable batch analyzer; and
  * a PyQt6 GUI annotator for interactive segmentation, tracking and review.

If you use this software, please cite both the OrganoID paper above and the
associated organoid-chip manuscript (see CITATION.cff).
